TPM Driver License Notice
=========================

The TPM TIS driver implementation in tpm2_driver.c is adapted from the
Linux kernel TPM subsystem, specifically understanding the TIS protocol
flow from drivers/char/tpm/tpm_tis_core.c.

Original Linux TPM driver:
  Copyright (C) 2005, 2006 IBM Corporation
  Copyright (C) 2014, 2015 Intel Corporation
  Authors: Leendert van Doorn, Kylene Hall
  License: GPL-2.0-only
  Source: https://github.com/torvalds/linux (v6.11)

This adapted implementation for Lux9:
  - Understands TIS register protocol from Linux reference
  - Reimplemented in Plan 9 C style without Linux dependencies
  - Uses Plan 9 kernel primitives (microdelay, print, etc.)
  - Simplified for embedded kernel use (no interrupts, no sysfs)
  - License: GPL-2.0-only (compatible with Linux sources)

The adaptation process:
1. Studied Linux TIS protocol implementation
2. Extracted core TIS register operations
3. Reimplemented using Plan 9 kernel APIs
4. Removed Linux-specific infrastructure (wait queues, sysfs, etc.)

This file maintains GPL-2.0 compliance for the TPM subsystem while
the rest of Lux9 kernel uses MIT/LPL/GPLv2+ licensing.
